{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/671234-what-does-it-mean-that-the-dreaming-is-dying","id":671234,"title":"What does it mean that the Dreaming is dying?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-19T13:26:56-07:00","id":671234,"title":"What does it mean that the Dreaming is dying?","content":"What has changed about humanity from over a thousand years ago that would cause the Dreaming to go from healthy to dying? Is it the lack of superstition? Actively disbelieving in spirit worlds? Less art? More knowledge, thus fewer places to insert a God of the gaps (or Fae of the gaps)? Considering how much the past sucked, and how hopeless the situation was back then, I am not sure what it is that is killing the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T13:46:44-07:00","id":671266,"title":"","content":"we are becoming more like weaver tainted mindless robots without creativity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T14:07:04-07:00","id":671290,"title":"","content":"How so? Was everyone an artist back in the day? Or are our lives too safe and stable now to imbue the Dreaming with the chaos and change needed to survive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T14:38:32-07:00","id":671344,"title":"","content":"The general idea is when the world was young and new, wonder and mystery was everywhere. As mankind grew larger in number, settled in more places, and became more in control of its own future (with new technology, improved social institutions, economic growth and prosperity), the land of the Fae become less and less accessible and the Fae race started to die.<br /> <br /> Think of it simply that humanity and the fae are competitors. As humanity thrives and expands, it is pushing out the area the fae can claim their own in the same way the coming of cro-magnon man displaced the neanderthals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T15:07:02-07:00","id":671354,"title":"","content":"No one knows and there doesn't seem to be a single clear cause. Some theories include the secret cabal of Grey men(aka Lets have the Technocracy/weaver etc crossover into our game). the natural cycle, just as their is a spring to things, there is a summer an Autumn and soon comes winter but spring will come again its just how things are. The Newest theory post the most recent DA book, The fae broke it they broke their world and its been dying ever since it became the Dreaming to survive and that wasn't enough to deal with the wounds that their stupid little war caused.<br /> <br /> And of course there's &quot;RAAAAWR SCIENCE BAD!&quot; which is kind of stupid and keys in iwth the crossover but there are at least some books that point that out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T16:07:35-07:00","id":671405,"title":"","content":"How did they break their world? This sounds fascinating. Also, is there any way to save it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T16:17:00-07:00","id":671441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/671234-what-does-it-mean-that-the-dreaming-is-dying?p=671405#post671405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did they break their world? This sounds fascinating. Also, is there any way to save it?</div> </div> </div> </div>DA fae starts with a Treaty between the Four seasonal courts that is supposed to end and return things to a state of war with the eclipse(or maybe it would be extended but this time line nope) so, Christian faith was inherently damaging to faery things unless you were a very powerful fae. So as they were about to go back to war one of the Fae comes up with the genius idea of weaponizing faith. othersides soon figure out what she did everyone starts mass dropping the equivalent of nukes on eachother so metaphorically the DA fae basically end up with a Mad Max scenario after the shattering.<br /> <br /> However they nuked eachother so hard they had to merge with the dreams of mankind to even survive so the ultimately end up retconning theirown lives and histories its why the Dreaming has a different timeline than DA fae.<br /> <br /> If that doesn't entirely make sense its because I can't quite grok it myself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T18:17:57-07:00","id":671568,"title":"","content":"Huh. This definitely puts the unfair martyrdom of House Liam in perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T23:39:26-07:00","id":671693,"title":"","content":"Meaning maybe those were the ones who first dropped the bomb, and the Dreaming turned them into pariahs as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T09:14:22-07:00","id":672061,"title":"","content":"DA Fae really didn't address the concept of houses AT ALL. It's all about the seasonal Courts. The Firstborn (most like the Sidhe) are usually in charge of most places, but not always. Sometimes its an Inanimae. Almost never a Changeling. <br /> <br /> There is no rational given, but it seems kinda like the Sidhe noble houses from CtDmay have formed AFTER the Sundering, mostly in Arcadia, kinda &quot;cults of personality&quot; around notable Firstborn. (I guess that would apply to House Scathach by having Scathach be the most notable Firstborn who remained and undertook the Changeling Way). At least, that's the best card toss into a hat I can come up with off the cuff. It seems to fit all the info, but probably not. DA Fae wasn't apparently really designed as a set-up for CtD overmuch. You can see the glimmers of CtD in there, but the systems don't match up so well. Neither do the &quot;stories&quot; (meaning what has been defined to be not metaplot, but is the plot built into the setting from the get-go, like Caine being the first vampire, and there being Antediluvians fighting each other by proxy through their childer - NOT metaplot, by Onyx Path definition). Except when they almost appear to, in twisty off-kilter ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T11:51:56-07:00","id":672257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> page 62 Darkening Sky</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Many fae who wish to fully re-kindle the War of Seasons<br /> attempt to recreate it, causing more Unleashings all over<br /> and seeking out baptized changelings to cripple their<br /> enemies. More and more fae become Lost, and the Mists<br /> react violently to the abuse to the point that Unleashing<br /> becomes nearly impossible in some places, especially<br /> human cities. The firstborn find it more difficult to hide<br /> in the Mists and have to find other means to conceal<br /> themselves, if not retreat into faerie realms completely.<br /> Changelings feel the sting of this less keenly, as they can<br /> more naturally walk among humanity.<br /> <br /> In an effort to adapt, some fae try to use cantrips for the<br /> same effect of the Friar\u2019s Cross, especially changelings. With<br /> the imposition of order and structure, the fae themselves<br /> become less varied, taking on Features similar to one<br /> another that are shaped by the dreams and nightmares of<br /> humanity. This gives rise to different kiths of changelings.<br /> When the Oath-Truce falls, the Shattering begins.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Entireity of how DA becomes Changeling from DA's perspective. I would argue that the war the Shattering so breaks the world that the past is lost and replaced with a new past the one of the Dreaming. That's why they don't match up the Fae broke their world hard and the dreams of man have twisted them greatly.<br /> <br /> Its why even if a changeling could travel back all they would see is the Dreaming.. though other creatures might find the other timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 09-20-2015, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T21:44:40-07:00","id":698393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/671234-what-does-it-mean-that-the-dreaming-is-dying#post671234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What has changed about humanity from over a thousand years ago that would cause the Dreaming to go from healthy to dying? Is it the lack of superstition? Actively disbelieving in spirit worlds? Less art? More knowledge, thus fewer places to insert a God of the gaps (or Fae of the gaps)? Considering how much the past sucked, and how hopeless the situation was back then, I am not sure what it is that is killing the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dreaming isn't dying per se. Rather, humanity's embrace of the certainty of Banality (over the wildness of Glamour) is homogenizing it, turning it into a sterile replica of mundane reality.<br /> <br /> As for why . . .even the fae themselves don't fully understand everything that happened. However, the Shattering (which forced the fae to flee to Arcadia, or go changeling) occurred roughly around the same time as the other splats embraced &quot;plausible deniability&quot;. The vampires set up the Masquerade, the Technocracy begins the Pogrom, Charon imposes the Dictuum Mortum . . . all of which involve convincing (or outright brainwashing) mundane humans that there <i>are</i> no supernatural beings in the world<br /> <br /> And that's likely something that humanity was all too ready to believe. The World of Darkness is terrible enough with just the &quot;real&quot; supernaturals - why add more horrors to it? As a force, Glamour is amoral - all it cares about is the potency of the dream/inspiration, regardless of whether that results in something wondrous or nightmarish. So, for a mundane human, buying into the new pro-Banality worldview makes sense. Being eaten by a rogue (Garou) werewolf is bad enough - why dream up a giant firebreathing (chimerical) one with three heads?<br /> <br /> Sure, that's filling the Dreaming with the metaphysical equivalent of gray sludge . . . but who knows? The greater the threat, the greater the victory. Maybe the current state of affairs is simply building up to the climax of the greatest epic in millennia, when humanity takes back the world from their supernatural overlords. Not much consolation for the fae and chimera who get plowed under in the meantime . . . but that's the way the Dreaming (and a good story) works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: On a side note, the spread of Banality (and the withering of the &quot;pro-fae&quot; sections of the Dreaming) is probably helping a lot of mental patients. Again, Glamour only considers the intensity of a dream . . . .and the delusions &amp; night terrors of the mad are often quite potent. Plus, many mentally ill individuals often have &quot;low&quot; Banality scores - leaving them vulnerable to monsters literally born from their worst nightmares. Monsters that modern pharmaceuticals (or therapy) can't protect them against","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 10-12-2015, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T13:28:38-07:00","id":701267,"title":"","content":"I am mostly in agreement with One Vorlon. However I would say that mortals have embraced a fatalistic view and expect the worst out of everyone and everything. A ravaged world in other words. This has made the Dreaming increasingly nightmare-oriented.<br /> <br /> In my home campaign(s) the Dreaming as encountered by the Fae is woven from the dreams of Earth mortals, but also by the denizens of other worlds, parallel dimensions and the Umbrood themselves. Planetary Incarnae and beings of the Outer Dark all contribute to the Dreaming. However these are very strange dreams and can be very difficult to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T15:42:35-07:00","id":701349,"title":"","content":"The Dreaming is actually the last refuge of the Mythic, tucked away in the dreams of mortals. So it's a kind of symbiosis between dreams and myth. The dream part is still there, but becoming dominated by nightmares and stasis. The Mythic part is so weak it can't exist for long outside of dreams. Either way, neither part is very healthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T07:27:03-07:00","id":702067,"title":"","content":"The Dreaming is a series of Oneiric Realms constructed by the (Jaggling) Umbrood known as the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oneiroi\" target=\"_blank\">Oneiroi </a>from the dreams of mortals. In essence these Umbrood are much like the &quot;Great Ones&quot; from H.P. Lovecraft's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream_Cycle\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Cycle</a>. Omnipotent in their home realm, but not very powerful outside of it. Dream Realms are pretty unstable for the most part, but if they are linked with bigger mythic concepts, they can hold together and even grow quite strong. But this course separates them more and more from the Superego, clinging to the Ego and Id of mankind.<br /> <br /> Another &quot;dying&quot; aspect of the Dreaming is that for centuries a number of powerful entities (Fomorians, K'llasshaa, etc) have been held back from the Mortal World (and mans Superego) by the magics of the Dreaming. Now as Banality has been steadily eating away at the Dreaming, those magical bonds are weakening. As these things get increasing access to mans innermost self, the world and its dreams get darker...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T05:38:13-07:00","id":706677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/671234-what-does-it-mean-that-the-dreaming-is-dying#post671234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What has changed about humanity from over a thousand years ago that would cause the Dreaming to go from healthy to dying? Is it the lack of superstition? Actively disbelieving in spirit worlds? Less art? More knowledge, thus fewer places to insert a God of the gaps (or Fae of the gaps)? Considering how much the past sucked, and how hopeless the situation was back then, I am not sure what it is that is killing the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well I think it would mean the death of magic in general, since in oWoD, reality is defined by consensus. If humanity is no longer able to think of new possibilities, then our scientific progress would come to a screeching halt. There would be no new discoveries or theories, only what we have previously discovered and believe to be true. Ironically, when the Technocracy freed the Fae by accident, they may have just saved their entire operation.<br /> <br /> Life would become stagnant and repetitive. Nothing ever changes, nothing ever progresses. Nobody has any motivation or hopes for the future.<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah, not a good thing to let humanity's imagination die.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/671234-what-does-it-mean-that-the-dreaming-is-dying?p=671354#post671354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And of course there's &quot;RAAAAWR SCIENCE BAD!&quot; which is kind of stupid</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, I like the whole fight against science and humanity in general concept some of the oWoD had. It reminds me a lot about Avatar, where the aliens have a miraculously deep connection to the world around them that redefines biology and the concept of a soul, then in comes humanity who's willing to destroy everything just to get some damn ore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-18-2015, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}